{
  "top_name": "cordic_sincos",
  "modules": [
    {
      "name": "cordic_prerot",
      "behavior": "Combinational CORDIC quadrant pre-rotation. Formats (all two's complement, ports unsigned bit vectors): angle is a 16-bit binary angle, theta = angle * 2*pi / 2^16 radians (one turn = 2^16); x and y are 18-bit Q2.16 (value / 2^16); z and atan values are 20-bit in units of 2^-20 turn; cos_out and sin_out are 16-bit Q2.14 (value / 2^14). K = 39797 = round(2^16 * prod_{i=0..15} 1/sqrt(1 + 2^-2i)). Quadrant q = angle[15:14]. When q is 01 or 10 (|theta| >= pi/2) the start vector is rotated by half a turn: x0 = -K (2^18 - 39797) and the reduced angle is angle ^ 0x8000; otherwise x0 = K and the reduced angle is angle. z0 = sign-extended reduced angle * 16, i.e. {reduced[15:0], 4'b0000}, a 20-bit value in 2^-20 turns within [-2^18, 2^18). The start vector's y is 0 (not a port). Python oracle: combinational and stateless; step returns the outputs for this step's inputs (latency 0, no clock and no reset port).",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "angle",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 16,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "x0",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 18,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "z0",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 20,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        }
      ],
      "latency": 0,
      "latency_known": true,
      "compare_mode": "fixed_latency",
      "reset": {
        "signal": "rst",
        "kind": "sync",
        "active_high": true,
        "duration_cycles": 3
      },
      "parameters": {},
      "clock_domains": [
        "clk"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "inputs": {
            "angle": 8192
          },
          "expected": {
            "x0": 39797,
            "z0": 131072
          },
          "after_cycles": 1
        },
        {
          "inputs": {
            "angle": 24576
          },
          "expected": {
            "x0": 222347,
            "z0": 917504
          },
          "after_cycles": 1
        },
        {
          "inputs": {
            "angle": 40960
          },
          "expected": {
            "x0": 222347,
            "z0": 131072
          },
          "after_cycles": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "cordic_atan",
      "behavior": "Combinational CORDIC arctangent table: atan = round(atan(2^-idx) / (2*pi) * 2^20), round half up, in 2^-20 turn units, for idx 0..15: 131072, 77376, 40884, 20753, 10417, 5213, 2607, 1304, 652, 326, 163, 81, 41, 20, 10, 5. Python oracle: combinational and stateless; step returns the outputs for this step's inputs (latency 0, no clock and no reset port).",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "idx",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 4,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "atan",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 20,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        }
      ],
      "latency": 0,
      "latency_known": true,
      "compare_mode": "fixed_latency",
      "reset": {
        "signal": "rst",
        "kind": "sync",
        "active_high": true,
        "duration_cycles": 3
      },
      "parameters": {},
      "clock_domains": [
        "clk"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "inputs": {
            "idx": 0
          },
          "expected": {
            "atan": 131072
          },
          "after_cycles": 1
        },
        {
          "inputs": {
            "idx": 3
          },
          "expected": {
            "atan": 20753
          },
          "after_cycles": 1
        },
        {
          "inputs": {
            "idx": 15
          },
          "expected": {
            "atan": 5
          },
          "after_cycles": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "cordic_engine",
      "behavior": "Iterative CORDIC rotation engine, one micro-rotation per rising edge, 16 iterations, with valid/ready-style handshake ports carried as plain protocol none signals. Formats (all two's complement, ports unsigned bit vectors): angle is a 16-bit binary angle, theta = angle * 2*pi / 2^16 radians (one turn = 2^16); x and y are 18-bit Q2.16 (value / 2^16); z and atan values are 20-bit in units of 2^-20 turn; cos_out and sin_out are 16-bit Q2.14 (value / 2^14). Registers, all reset to 0: busy, out_valid, i[3:0], x[17:0], y[17:0], z[19:0]. Outputs, all views of registered state: in_ready = !busy && !out_valid; out_valid; iter = i; x; y. atan_val is the table value for index iter (from the atan table neighbour); x0 and z0 come from the pre-rotation of the input angle. At each rising edge with rst low, using pre-edge values: if busy: with xs = x >>> i and ys = y >>> i (arithmetic shifts of the 18-bit two's complement values, rounding toward minus infinity), if z >= 0 (z[19] = 0) then x = x - ys, y = y + xs, z = z - atan_val, else x = x + ys, y = y - xs, z = z + atan_val (x and y modulo 2^18, z modulo 2^20); i = i + 1 modulo 16; and when i was 15, busy = 0 and out_valid = 1. Else if out_valid: out_valid = 0 when out_ready = 1 (x and y hold). Else (idle) if in_valid = 1: accept: x = x0, y = 0, z = z0, i = 0, busy = 1. in_valid, x0 and z0 are ignored except at the accepting edge. An accepted angle takes 16 busy edges and out_valid appears after the 16th; the next angle can be accepted at the edge after the output transfer at the earliest. Synchronous active-high rst at a rising edge returns every register to its reset value; reset has no effect between edges. Python oracle: cycle-level model, one step per rising edge; keep the registers in state and return every output as it is after that edge. The driver applies the fixed latency of 1; do not add a delay queue. init() is the reset state and a supplied rst must be handled.",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "clk",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "rst",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "in_valid",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "in_ready",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 1,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "x0",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 18,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "z0",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 20,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "atan_val",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 20,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "iter",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 4,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "out_valid",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 1,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "out_ready",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "x",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 18,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "y",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 18,
          "protocol": "none",
          "signed": false
        }
      ],
      "latency": 1,
      "latency_known": true,
      "compare_mode": "fixed_latency",
      "reset": {
        "signal": "rst",
        "kind": "sync",
        "active_high": true,
        "duration_cycles": 3
      },
      "parameters": {},
      "clock_domains": [
        "clk"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "inputs": {
            "rst": 0,
            "in_valid": 1,
            "x0": 39797,
            "z0": 131072,
            "atan_val": 131072,
            "out_ready": 0
          },
          "expected": {
            "in_ready": 0,
            "iter": 1,
            "out_valid": 0,
            "x": 39797,
            "y": 39797
          },
          "after_cycles": 2
        },
        {
          "inputs": {
            "rst": 0,
            "in_valid": 1,
            "x0": 39797,
            "z0": 131072,
            "atan_val": 20753,
            "out_ready": 0
          },
          "expected": {
            "in_ready": 0,
            "iter": 0,
            "out_valid": 1,
            "x": 252246,
            "y": 64781
          },
          "after_cycles": 17
        },
        {
          "inputs": {
            "rst": 0,
            "in_valid": 1,
            "x0": 222347,
            "z0": 983040,
            "atan_val": 5213,
            "out_ready": 1
          },
          "expected": {
            "in_ready": 0,
            "iter": 1,
            "out_valid": 0,
            "x": 222347,
            "y": 39797
          },
          "after_cycles": 20
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "cordic_out",
      "behavior": "Combinational CORDIC output stage: Q2.16 to Q2.14 with round half up. cos_out = ((x_in + 2) >>> 2) and sin_out = ((y_in + 2) >>> 2), where x_in and y_in are 18-bit two's complement, the sum is formed without overflow (19 bits) and the result is its low 16 bits (bits [17:2] of the 19-bit sum, wrapping for out-of-range inputs that the engine never produces). Python oracle: combinational and stateless; step returns the outputs for this step's inputs (latency 0, no clock and no reset port).",
      "ports": [
